    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148-a1">

                <pb facs="0142" n="132" xml:id="pg132"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Draft of Note From the Netherlands Consular
                        Representative at Peiping to Mr. Chou En-lai </hi>
                </head>
                <p>The new situation resulting from the recent formation of the Central People’s
                    Government forms an object of careful study by the Netherlands Government.</p>
                <p>With a view to continuing the friendly relations which have always existed
                    between the Netherlands and China, the Netherlands Government suggests that,
                    pending completing of its study, the Netherlands consular officers in the
                    territory under the control of the Central People’s Government take up informal
                    contacts with the local authorities. In the opinion of the Netherlands
                    Government such a provisional arrangement may contribute to the promotion of
                    mutual trade and would be advantageous for both Governments.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d148-f1"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d148-f1" n="29" xml:id="d148-f1-content">
                <p>On November 1 the Department was informed by the Netherlands Embassy that the
                    last word of this draft was changed from “Governments” to “peoples”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
